@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il27-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il27-tax-years`
IMPORT `ito-s47a-national-insurance-deduction`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Tests for s 47A. Row IL-27. Expected values worked by hand from lines 1792-1797 before the rules were run; none edited.
-- Deduction = 52% of (contributions paid less the s 179(a) addition) [less a refund, from tax year 2025], not above the taxable income before it.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Tests — section 47A`

-- The fields: tax year; contributions on income that is not work income; on work income, the employer not liable; the s 179(a) addition included;
-- a refund received; taxable income before the deduction; medical insurance sums.
GIVEN `the year`   IS A NUMBER
      `non-work`   IS A NUMBER
      `work`       IS A NUMBER
      `addition`   IS A NUMBER
      `refund`     IS A NUMBER
      `income`     IS A NUMBER
      `medical`    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `National Insurance contributions in a tax year, for section 47A`
`in` `the year` `: contributions on other income` `non-work` `, on work income` `work` `, of which addition` `addition` `, refund` `refund` `, taxable income` `income` `, medical sums` `medical` MEANS
    `National Insurance contributions in a tax year, for section 47A` OF `the year`, `non-work`, `work`, `addition`, `refund`, `income`, `medical`

§§ `(a) and (b)`

-- 20,000 paid on income that is not work income: 52% x 20,000 = 10,400. Taxable income 300,000, far above.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47A for` (`in` 2026 `: contributions on other income` 20000 `, on work income` 0 `, of which addition` 0 `, refund` 0 `, taxable income` 300000 `, medical sums` 0) EQUALS 10400
-- With 1,000 of the 20,000 an addition under s 179(a): 19,000 -> 52% = 9,880.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47A for` (`in` 2026 `: contributions on other income` 20000 `, on work income` 0 `, of which addition` 1000 `, refund` 0 `, taxable income` 300000 `, medical sums` 0) EQUALS 9880
-- (b): 10,000 paid on work income by one whose employer is not liable, 5,000 on other income: 15,000 -> 52% = 7,800.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47A for` (`in` 2026 `: contributions on other income` 5000 `, on work income` 10000 `, of which addition` 0 `, refund` 0 `, taxable income` 300000 `, medical sums` 0) EQUALS 7800
-- The cap at taxable income: income 5,000 and 20,000 paid (10,400 > 5,000): 5,000. Income exactly 10,400: 10,400. Income 10,399: 10,399.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47A for` (`in` 2026 `: contributions on other income` 20000 `, on work income` 0 `, of which addition` 0 `, refund` 0 `, taxable income` 5000 `, medical sums` 0) EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47A for` (`in` 2026 `: contributions on other income` 20000 `, on work income` 0 `, of which addition` 0 `, refund` 0 `, taxable income` 10400 `, medical sums` 0) EQUALS 10400
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47A for` (`in` 2026 `: contributions on other income` 20000 `, on work income` 0 `, of which addition` 0 `, refund` 0 `, taxable income` 10399 `, medical sums` 0) EQUALS 10399
-- Nothing paid: nothing. Before 2024: refused.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47A for` (`in` 2026 `: contributions on other income` 0 `, on work income` 0 `, of which addition` 0 `, refund` 0 `, taxable income` 300000 `, medical sums` 0) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `the deduction under section 47A for` (`in` 2023 `: contributions on other income` 20000 `, on work income` 0 `, of which addition` 0 `, refund` 0 `, taxable income` 300000 `, medical sums` 0) BECAUSE "row IL-27 does not hold the text of these sections for a tax year before 2024"

§§ `(b1) — a refund, from tax year 2025`

-- 2026: 20,000 paid, 4,000 refunded: 52% x 16,000 = 8,320. In 2024 (b1) did not exist: the refund is not looked at, 10,400.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47A for` (`in` 2026 `: contributions on other income` 20000 `, on work income` 0 `, of which addition` 0 `, refund` 4000 `, taxable income` 300000 `, medical sums` 0) EQUALS 8320
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47A for` (`in` 2025 `: contributions on other income` 20000 `, on work income` 0 `, of which addition` 0 `, refund` 4000 `, taxable income` 300000 `, medical sums` 0) EQUALS 8320
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47A for` (`in` 2024 `: contributions on other income` 20000 `, on work income` 0 `, of which addition` 0 `, refund` 4000 `, taxable income` 300000 `, medical sums` 0) EQUALS 10400
-- A refund larger than the contributions: paid 3,000, refunded 5,000. 2026: no deduction, and 52% x 2,000 = 1,040 is business income.
-- 2024: the refund is not looked at, 52% x 3,000 = 1,560 deducted and nothing deemed.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47A for` (`in` 2026 `: contributions on other income` 3000 `, on work income` 0 `, of which addition` 0 `, refund` 5000 `, taxable income` 300000 `, medical sums` 0) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the income deemed to be from a business or profession under section 47A(b1) for` (`in` 2026 `: contributions on other income` 3000 `, on work income` 0 `, of which addition` 0 `, refund` 5000 `, taxable income` 300000 `, medical sums` 0) EQUALS 1040
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47A for` (`in` 2024 `: contributions on other income` 3000 `, on work income` 0 `, of which addition` 0 `, refund` 5000 `, taxable income` 300000 `, medical sums` 0) EQUALS 1560
#ASSERT `the income deemed to be from a business or profession under section 47A(b1) for` (`in` 2024 `: contributions on other income` 3000 `, on work income` 0 `, of which addition` 0 `, refund` 5000 `, taxable income` 300000 `, medical sums` 0) EQUALS 0
-- A refund equal to the contributions: nothing deducted and nothing deemed.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47A for` (`in` 2026 `: contributions on other income` 3000 `, on work income` 0 `, of which addition` 0 `, refund` 3000 `, taxable income` 300000 `, medical sums` 0) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the income deemed to be from a business or profession under section 47A(b1) for` (`in` 2026 `: contributions on other income` 3000 `, on work income` 0 `, of which addition` 0 `, refund` 3000 `, taxable income` 300000 `, medical sums` 0) EQUALS 0

§§ `Fork F9a — does (a)'s cap survive (b1)?`

-- Income 5,000, 20,000 paid, 1,000 refunded: 52% x 19,000 = 9,880 against a cap of 5,000. The cap applies: 5,000; it does not: 9,880; the default declines.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47A, reading the cap in (b1) as` `the cap of subsection (a) applies` `and subsection (c) as` `subsection (c) lapses with the Parallel Tax Law` `, for` (`in` 2026 `: contributions on other income` 20000 `, on work income` 0 `, of which addition` 0 `, refund` 1000 `, taxable income` 5000 `, medical sums` 0) EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47A, reading the cap in (b1) as` `the cap of subsection (a) does not apply` `and subsection (c) as` `subsection (c) lapses with the Parallel Tax Law` `, for` (`in` 2026 `: contributions on other income` 20000 `, on work income` 0 `, of which addition` 0 `, refund` 1000 `, taxable income` 5000 `, medical sums` 0) EQUALS 9880
#ASSERT REFUSED `the deduction under section 47A for` (`in` 2026 `: contributions on other income` 20000 `, on work income` 0 `, of which addition` 0 `, refund` 1000 `, taxable income` 5000 `, medical sums` 0) BECAUSE "section 47A(b1) does not say whether the cap of subsection (a) on the deduction survives it, and here the cap decides"
-- With no refund (a) governs with its cap and nothing is declined: 5,000. Where the cap does not bind, the default answers.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47A for` (`in` 2026 `: contributions on other income` 20000 `, on work income` 0 `, of which addition` 0 `, refund` 0 `, taxable income` 5000 `, medical sums` 0) EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `section 47A — the reading row IL-27 takes of the cap in subsection (b1)` EQUALS `declined where the cap decides`

§§ `Fork F9 — (c), after the Parallel Tax Law`

-- 2,000 of medical insurance sums. The default declines; (c) lapsing adds nothing; (c) surviving has no cap in the text.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the deduction under section 47A for` (`in` 2026 `: contributions on other income` 20000 `, on work income` 0 `, of which addition` 0 `, refund` 0 `, taxable income` 300000 `, medical sums` 2000) BECAUSE "section 47A(c) does not say whether it survives subsection (d) for a tax year after 1996, and here medical insurance sums were paid"
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47A, reading the cap in (b1) as` `the cap of subsection (a) applies` `and subsection (c) as` `subsection (c) lapses with the Parallel Tax Law` `, for` (`in` 2026 `: contributions on other income` 20000 `, on work income` 0 `, of which addition` 0 `, refund` 0 `, taxable income` 300000 `, medical sums` 2000) EQUALS 10400
#ASSERT REFUSED `the deduction under section 47A, reading the cap in (b1) as` `the cap of subsection (a) applies` `and subsection (c) as` `subsection (c) survives` `, for` (`in` 2026 `: contributions on other income` 20000 `, on work income` 0 `, of which addition` 0 `, refund` 0 `, taxable income` 300000 `, medical sums` 2000) BECAUSE "section 47A(c) caps the deduction at the parallel tax that would have applied, and the Parallel Tax Law applies to no tax year after 1996, so the text gives no cap"
-- No medical sums: nothing to decide, and the default answers.
#ASSERT `section 47A — the reading row IL-27 takes of subsection (c)` EQUALS `declined where medical insurance sums were paid`
